From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:22:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] H3: interpreter work budget and nesting cap for nested
 contexts

Add `InterpretBudget` to `InterpreterSettings`: an optional operator
limit and an optional deadline, checked every `check_interval` (default
4096) operators. `interpret()` counts each operator and stops once the
budget is exhausted; enclosing interpretations stop at their next
operator. `draw_form_xobject`, Type3 glyph procedures, tiling patterns
and soft masks return early when it is exhausted.

The budget's counters live behind an `Arc` that clones share, so the
fresh contexts hayro builds for Type3 glyphs, patterns and soft masks
(from a clone of the settings) count against the same limit. The state
is always allocated; the default budget has no limits and only counts.
`Context::stats()` returns `InterpretStats` (operators, exhaustion
reason, nesting-cap hits) and `Context::budget_exhausted()`.

Type3 glyphs, tiling patterns and soft masks recorded a nesting depth
but never checked it, so a Type3 glyph showing itself recursed until the
stack overflowed under a device that runs glyph procedures. They now
apply the 50-level cap that forms use, and every refusal is counted.
